<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n38289" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπάρᾱτος</span></b> 
		<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">[ᾰρ]</span>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>, (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπαράομαι</span>) <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>accursed, laid under a curse,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐ. ποιεῖσθαι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Th.
					8.97
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὃ ἐπάρατον ἦν μὴ
			οἰκεῖν</span> which it was <i>accursed</i> to inhabit, <i><span class="en">
				Id.
				2.17
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τῷ δὲ ἐπάρατον τύχην
			[γενέσθαι</span>] <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Lg.</u>
				877a
			</span></i>; of persons, <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
			</span></i>(?) <i><span class="en">
				<u>Fr.</u>
				148
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Ev.Jo.</u>
				7.49
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				J.
				<u>AJ</u>
				6.6.3
			</span></i>: 
				Sup.
			, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">γενεά</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Ph.
					1.516
				</span></i>
			; used in imprecations on those who violated graves, <i><span class="en">
				<u>CIG</u>
				2824
			</span></i> (<span class="entity">Aphrodisias</span>), etc.</div>
